  <ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock id="Tag206" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: .25in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: black;"&gt;1/3. Southwest Gas Transmission Company (the Company) is a natural gas company as defined by the Natural Gas Act (52 Stat. 821, 15 U.S.C. 717-717W) and, as such, is subject to the jurisdiction of the FERC. There were no important changes in the scope of the Company&amp;#8217;s operations during the current year.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: .25in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: black;"&gt;2. The Company&amp;#8217;s pipeline consists of approximately nine miles of 20-inch O.D. pipe from the northwest one-quarter, Section 17, Township 18 North, Range 21 West, Mojave County, Arizona, to the southern most receipt point of the Southwest Gas Corporation southern Nevada mainline located in the middle of the Colorado River approximately three miles north of the common boundary of Arizona, Nevada, and California.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock>
